Practical problem 3 (59 points / 11% of the total). Beauty in simplicity

[Chemicals and equipment for Problem 3: Beauty in Simplicity. Chemical: solutions S1-S6, liquid, corrosive, in vials labeled "S1"/"S2"/"S3"/"S4"/"S5"/"S6" + "[student code]" (the GHS hazard codes printed in the list are omitted).]

$$\begin{array}{l|c} \text{Item} & \text{Count} \\ \hline \text{Bottle (100 mL), labeled "Waste (P3)"} & 1 \\ \text{Sample vials (20 mL), labeled "S1"/"S2"/"S3"/"S4"/"S5"/"S6" + "[student code]"} & 6 \\ \text{Test tubes} & 18 \\ \text{Glass Pasteur pipettes} & 10 \\ \text{Test tube rack} & 1 \end{array}$$

Introduction

You are provided with 6 solutions S1–S6 (ca. 10 mL of each) of unknown composition. Solution Sx is labeled "[student code] + Sx", with x going from 1 to 6. Your task is to identify all cations and anions dissolved in these solutions.

Hints:

• There are 7 cations and 7 anions which have been introduced in aqueous solutions S1–S6 from the list:
• Cations: $\ce{Ag+}$, $\ce{Ba^{2+}}$, $\ce{Ca^{2+}}$, $\ce{Fe^{3+}}$, $\ce{K+}$, $\ce{Mn^{2+}}$, $\ce{Na+}$;
• Anions: $\ce{CH3COO-}$, $\ce{Cl-}$, $\ce{I-}$, $\ce{NO3-}$, $\ce{PO4^{3-}}$, $\ce{S^{2-}}$, $\ce{SO4^{2-}}$;
• 2 or 3 ions in total were introduced into each solution;
• Each of the ions was introduced only into one solution;
• $\ce{Na+}$ and $\ce{K+}$ are present together in the same solution;
• In some cases, it might take up to 15 minutes before a visible change occurs; fill in the table in question 3.1 with your final observations;
• Some solutions can get colored or attain some precipitate due to oxidation under air.

Questions

3.1 (30 pt) Perform the cross-reactions between solutions S1–S6. Fill in the first table of your answer sheet with your observations using these symbols:

• "↓" for precipitation;
• "↑" for gas evolution;
• " S " for colour change of the solution;
• " – " if there are no visible observations.

Report the colours of the precipitates using the following letters:

• " W " for white/colorless;
• " B " for black;
• " C " for colored.

